 generic realism rather than class transfer. Overall, CounterFlow achieves state-of-the-art counterfactual validity and the best realism/proximity trade-off on CIFAR-10, while substantially reducing inference complexity compared with prior flow- and diffusion-based approaches. Ablation. Table 1(b) shows that replacing latent-space pairing with random pairing consistently lowers conditional validity and raises both target and source FID on both datasets, mostly through the source FID on CIFAR-10. Pairing semantically similar examples yields simpler transport trajectories that are easier for the conditional velocity field to approximate, whereas random pairing often associates visually unrelated samples, leading to harder-to-learn trajectories and lower-quality counterfactuals. Section A.3 further ablates λ \lambda , the conditioning context and the explained classifier. 5.3 Qualitative Results Style Preservation. Figure 1 shows five source/counterfactual pairs per data
